{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I will make you into nations</b> — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 17:6): Israel and Edom, since Ishmael was already his and He would not be announcing about him. But it does not seem correct to me that at the time of the covenant of circumcision He would announce about Esau, when he does not fulfill circumcision and was not even commanded concerning it, as they expounded in Sanhedrin (59a): \"For through Isaac\" — and not all of Isaac. Rather, Israel alone are called גוים (nations) and עמים (peoples), and likewise \"Indeed, He loves the peoples\" (Deuteronomy 33:3), \"Peoples, He calls to the mountain\" (Deuteronomy 33:19), \"After you, Benjamin, among your peoples\" (Judges 5:14). Also, after the tribes were all born, He said: \"A nation and a company of nations shall come from you\" (Genesis 35:11), \"And I will make you a company of peoples\" (Genesis 48:4)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:11.661967139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}